    dc:description "Modern data can test genetic variation and inheritance for selected behaviours. They do not broadly quantify the historical balance between selection and inherited habit across complex instincts.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For instinctive behaviours with known pedigrees or genomic data, estimate heritable variation, selection, and transgenerational effects of acquired habits. Predominant response through heritable variants rather than inherited acquired behaviour supports the claim.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Public behaviour datasets rarely combine pedigrees, selection, and transgenerational experiments.", "Relative historical contributions are difficult to reconstruct.";
